Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

POST /api/portal/recover takes the surname and phone given at purchase.
The server finds the cabinet and sends the code only where the client
connected themselves: the Telegram bot and email. The code is never
returned to the browser, and the answer is the same whether a cabinet
exists or not, so the form cannot tell who studies with us. Sending
happens after the answer.

If the cabinet has no Telegram or email, or sending failed, the owner
gets the code in the work chat to forward in WhatsApp by hand.

Limits: 5 requests per IP in 5 minutes, one send per cabinet in two
minutes, so the form cannot be used to flood someone's Telegram.

Orders also accept an optional email (manual and Stripe). It is
validated, kept on the order and copied to the cabinet on activation,
so recovery by email works from the first day. Without the field
everything works as before.

Tests: unit tests for matching, cooldown and delivery; server wiring
tests for recovery, owner alert, bad input and purchase email; smoke
checks for the new route. 95/95 and smoke 28/28 locally.

